  "contracts": [
    "Provider finalization is shared by CLI startup and workspace requests.",
    "Each query owns cancellation, limits, statistics and borrowed option lifetimes; every worker lease joins before release.",
    "File/provider worker pools retain at most 32 idle threads each; higher explicit concurrency can use temporary threads.",
    "HTTP connections and lazy native runtime survive compatible queries. Identity/cache/configuration changes retire the provider scope after workers join.",
    "32 MiB plan admission includes construction and evicted active leases, 4 MiB maximum per plan, ordinary fallback on admission failure.",
    "4 MiB batch payload memo keeps original timestamps; TTL validation occurs on each use.",
    "Each generation charges shared immutable source blobs in full; old generations are never chained.",
    "Source names borrow retained raw bytes when possible; synthesized names are owned and kind strings interned.",
    "Only coarse region metadata/keys are memoized; provider text materializes from the active pinned source when needed."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Sampled SDK physical footprint/peak increases from 79.9M to 97.8M; reduced CPU is a memory tradeoff, not an RSS win.",
    "Warm fixture benchmarks establish orchestration/evidence equivalence and CPU work reductions, not live-model quality or billing.",
    "Allocator and budgets match ordinary parser execution to preserve bounded outcomes.",
    "No new regex JIT paths; local controls remain mixed on a shared host.",
    "No automatic OS watcher, independent native Linux hardware timing, Windows runtime qualification or live-provider testing.",
    "PR CI remains subject to repository human-admission policy."
  ]
